   "text": {
    "L1": "A transversal crosses two lines and makes eight angles.",
    "L2": "Corresponding angles are in matching positions at the two crossings. Trace an F shape.",
    "L3": "Alternate angles lie between the lines on opposite sides of the transversal. Trace a Z shape.",
    "L4": "When the lines are parallel, corresponding angles are equal and alternate angles are equal.",
    "L5": "Interior angles on the same side add to 180 degrees, not equal angles.",
    "L6": "So equal corresponding angles can test that two lines are parallel.",
    "L7": "But if corresponding angles differ, the lines are not parallel. They will meet if extended.",
    "L8": "Now use the angle rules to choose the correct answer."
   },
